From 249ffe4d5aa5f4b88805dee0d635ab99f8f783d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sungsu Ahn <sungsu_ahn@korea.ac.kr>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:32:47 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 30/51] nr: replay flushes on the issuing node too (own
 events), slots and objects
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

User decision D4 (2026-10-15). Paper §3.4.3: "While replaying the log, if a
host finds an allocation or deallocation event, it flushes the CPU caches for
the affected objects"; NR replays the issuer's own entries as well (combine,
mine = true). Upstream (and the port so far) flushed only for !mine ops, so a
node's own RO switch (reclaim) could leave lines it had cached before another
node's write, and its next RO-path read skipped every check. exec_notify now
flushes the slot (or the object's range) for every replayed op that names one;
notification clearing is unchanged. This changes the slot path: each own op
whose response carries a cn index (admit, create, RO/RW switch, wrap-around)
now also flushes that slot on the issuer.

object_tests: an own event gives exactly one flush on the issuer and one on
the peer (was: none on the issuer).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
